insert into public.services(title,slug,short_description,description,benefits,features,image_url,seo_title,meta_description,published) values
('Residential Rooftop Solar','residential-solar','A rooftop plan shaped around your home, your bill and your roof.','A useful home solar proposal starts with more than a monthly bill. EXDELLS reviews the consumer connection, daily usage, usable roof area, shade, structure and cleaning access before discussing capacity. For Rajasthan properties, heat exposure and dust maintenance are part of the practical design conversation. The result is a site-specific scope with clear assumptions, utility coordination steps and a handover plan.','["Review recent bills and day-versus-evening usage","Check roof structure, shade, orientation and safe access","Compare on-grid and backup options against your actual needs","Understand current residential scheme steps, where eligible","Agree equipment, scope, approvals and handover"]','["On-grid rooftop solar","Hybrid systems where backup needs support them","Residential scheme guidance subject to eligibility"]','photo-1509391366360-2e959784a276','Residential Rooftop Solar in Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Rooftop solar planning for Rajasthan homes, with roof, usage, dust maintenance and utility requirements assessed.','true'),
('Commercial Solar EPC','commercial-solar','A practical energy plan for the way your facility operates.','Offices, retail properties, hotels, warehouses and campuses have different operating hours and load profiles. EXDELLS starts with bill or interval data where available, then reviews roof and electrical capacity, export conditions, site access and business continuity. The proposal makes assumptions and exclusions visible, so your team can compare options against the same scope.','["Map daytime demand and operating hours","Review roof, carport or suitable site area","Assess electrical integration and meter requirements","Plan access, work windows and safety coordination","Document scope, commercial assumptions and commissioning"]','["Rooftop and carport feasibility","Load and tariff review","Phased project planning"]','photo-1497366754035-f200968a6e72','Commercial Solar EPC Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Commercial solar EPC for Rajasthan offices, hotels, retail, warehouses and campuses; scope follows site assessment.','true'),
('Industrial Solar EPC','industrial-solar','Solar engineering aligned with production, safety and site constraints.','A plant cannot be treated like a generic roof. EXDELLS works through production shifts, process loads, shutdown windows, structural information, electrical diagrams and site safety rules before shaping an industrial EPC scope. System design is subject to structural and electrical engineering, utility requirements and detailed technical assessment.','["Understand shift patterns, load profile and expansion plans","Review structural drawings and roof condition","Coordinate electrical integration and protection design","Sequence work around operations and site safety","Define testing, documentation and handover requirements"]','["Industrial rooftop feasibility","Electrical integration planning","Project delivery coordination"]','photo-1486406146926-c627a92ad1ab','Industrial Solar EPC Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Industrial solar feasibility and EPC planning for Rajasthan plants, warehouses and operating facilities.','true'),
('On-grid Solar Systems','on-grid-solar','Generate solar power in coordination with your electricity connection.','An on-grid system is designed to operate alongside a utility supply. The right configuration depends on consumption, sanctioned load, connection type, roof conditions and the current interconnection process for the meter point. Standard grid-tied inverters shut down during a grid outage unless compliant backup equipment is designed into the system.','["Review the electricity connection and recent bills","Size against actual usage and available roof area","Confirm local DISCOM application and metering steps","Review anti-islanding and electrical protection scope","Explain monitoring and operating behaviour at handover"]','["Grid-connected inverter system","Interconnection planning","Monitoring and commissioning"]','photo-1509391366360-2e959784a276','On-grid Solar Systems Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Learn about grid-connected solar systems, DISCOM coordination and site-specific design in Rajasthan.','true'),
('Hybrid Solar Systems','hybrid-solar','Add storage for the loads that matter when the grid is unavailable.','Hybrid solar pairs a grid connection with solar generation and battery storage. The useful question is not “how large a battery?” but “which equipment needs to run, and for how long?” EXDELLS helps map critical circuits, starting currents, backup duration and battery location before comparing configurations.','["Create a priority-load list","Set a realistic backup duration","Check inverter changeover and starting-current needs","Plan battery placement, ventilation and access","Explain how storage changes system cost and operation"]','["Solar, battery and grid integration","Critical-load mapping","Backup operating-mode handover"]','photo-1473341304170-971dccb5ac1e','Hybrid Solar Systems Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Plan a hybrid solar and battery system around priority loads, backup duration and site conditions.','true'),
('Off-grid Solar Systems','off-grid-solar','A solar-and-storage design for sites without dependable grid supply.','Off-grid systems must serve the load through changing weather and operating conditions. A reliable design begins with an appliance inventory, duty cycles, seasonal demand and the autonomy required. Solar array, battery, inverter and any backup generator are sized together; a quick roof-area estimate is not enough.','["Inventory loads, duty cycles and critical equipment","Define autonomy and acceptable backup arrangements","Consider seasonal use and battery operating limits","Assess maintenance access and safe equipment placement","Provide operating guidance with commissioning"]','["Solar array and battery sizing","Inverter and backup integration","Operating and maintenance handover"]','photo-1508514177221-188b1cf16e9d','Off-grid Solar Systems Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Site-specific off-grid solar and storage planning for Rajasthan properties without dependable grid supply.','true'),
('PM Surya Ghar Guidance','pm-surya-ghar','Understand the rooftop process and what to verify before you commit.','For eligible residential consumers, PM Surya Ghar is administered through the current national scheme process and the DISCOM serving the electricity connection. EXDELLS can discuss technical readiness and questions to confirm. Registration, vendor eligibility, consumer documents, subsidy amount and timing must be checked on the official portal; scheme rules can change.','["Identify the DISCOM for the exact meter location","Review current eligibility and vendor requirements on the official portal","Check roof and system suitability before agreeing a scope","Keep application and installation details consistent","Track approval and commissioning requirements through official channels"]','["Residential scheme orientation","Rooftop suitability review","Application questions and installation planning"]','photo-1497435334941-8c899ee9e8e9','PM Surya Ghar Guidance Rajasthan | EXDELLS','Rajasthan rooftop solar guidance for eligible households. Verify current scheme and vendor rules on the official portal.','true')
