insert into public.blogs(title,slug,excerpt,content,author,category,status,published_at,seo_title,meta_description) values
('Rajasthan rooftop solar planning: dust, heat and the meter connection','rajasthan-rooftop-solar-planning','A Rajasthan rooftop project needs a site-specific look at heat exposure, dust maintenance, roof access and the utility connection serving the property.','Solar planning for Rajasthan starts with the property, not a single state-wide system size. Roof conditions, electricity use, temperature exposure, maintenance access and the consumer meter connection all affect the engineering and project process.\n\n## Plan around the roof and exposure\nRecord the roof material, condition, usable area, parapets, nearby shade and access. In a dry, dusty location, cleaning access and the owner’s safe maintenance plan deserve an early conversation. Module temperature and soiling can affect output, so a production estimate should use transparent assumptions rather than a headline annual figure.\n\n## Identify the distribution company for the meter\nA city name alone does not establish the utility route. Check the DISCOM and consumer details printed on the latest electricity bill, then verify the current application and metering steps through that utility and the official PM Surya Ghar portal where the residential scheme applies. Applications and scheme rules can change.\n\n## Size for how the property uses power\nA home, hotel, warehouse and factory may all have different peak hours and critical loads. Recent bills help, but operating hours and future plans add context. If backup is required, identify specific circuits and duration before sizing storage.\n\n## Ask for a Rajasthan-ready project scope\nThe proposal should explain the expected-generation method, system layout, mounting, equipment, electrical protections, utility coordination, cleaning access, commissioning checks, exclusions and after-sales route. The project scope should be confirmed after a site survey.\n\nThis guide is general information. Verify current local requirements and scheme eligibility against official channels before making a purchase decision.','EXDELLS Editorial','Rajasthan planning','published',now(),'Rajasthan Rooftop Solar Planning Guide | EXDELLS','Plan rooftop solar in Rajasthan with a site-specific review of dust, heat, roof access, usage and DISCOM requirements.')
